                                        "sense_id": "56ee4a9b-4f3e-346b-8ff9-973602903cd2",
                                        "entry_id": "0bb6cf7d-7726-3490-82af-e41ed2bcf632",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Communication, conversation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b71ec6c9-9ae9-4782-811c-408cd3b2e9b5",
                                                "sense_id": "56ee4a9b-4f3e-346b-8ff9-973602903cd2",
                                                "text": "Yet do I vnderſtand your darkeſt language, / Your treads ath'toe, your ſecret iogges and vvringes: / Your entercourſe of glaunces: euery tittle / Of your cloſe Amorous rites I vnderſtand, / They ſpeake as loud to mee, as if you ſaid, / My deareſt Dariotto, I am thine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c4717de-8493-42fd-a91a-3dc4cbc74a38",
                                                "sense_id": "56ee4a9b-4f3e-346b-8ff9-973602903cd2",
                                                "text": "this sweet intercourse of looks and smiles"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e9578aa-2172-4d37-abc4-7f5bd2328a7b",
                                                "sense_id": "56ee4a9b-4f3e-346b-8ff9-973602903cd2",
                                                "text": "And indeed, what more reliable authority could Berlioz have found than Cavaillé-Coll, with whom he had frequent intercourse, and who would have been better qualified than any one else to give him correct information?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "41c7aa7c-ac21-42a5-8799-114f996aab93",
                                                "sense_id": "56ee4a9b-4f3e-346b-8ff9-973602903cd2",
                                                "text": "It was a joy to snatch some brief respite, and find himself in the rectory drawing–room. Listening here was as pleasant as talking; just to watch was pleasant. The young priests who lived here wore cassocks and birettas; their faces were fine and mild, yet really strong, like the rector's face; and in their intercourse with him and his wife they seemed to be brothers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5720258c-7712-468c-9615-dab2872cd92b",
                                                "sense_id": "56ee4a9b-4f3e-346b-8ff9-973602903cd2",
                                                "text": "It might seem that with age places gained upon persons in interest to my mind; and that my pleasure grew in intercourse with things rather than with ideas."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d5adac1-5379-379b-95f2-8d1c8abd0cf1",
